# Formally per color c: consider the graph of c-cells. If c-cells contain a cycle, flood from border avoiding c; enclosed non-c cells become c. Also cells ON the cycle that were NOT c... no, cycle cells are all c by definition.
# Simpler operational version: cell (y,x) becomes c iff it lies inside or on a closed c-loop. Compute: for each color c, mark cell as "inside-or-on-loop" if removing... use: cell is inside-loop iff every path to border crosses c. Approximate via even-parity/point-in-polygon along rows (ray casting against c cells).
def solve(I, verbose=False):
    H,W=len(I),len(I[0])
    O=[row[:] for row in I]
    for y in range(H):
        for x in range(W):
            cval=I[y][x]
